 ## Overview
 
-Marching Tetrahedra is an isosurface extraction algorithm that decomposes each cubic voxel into tetrahedra to resolve the topological ambiguities inherent in [Marching Cubes](774-marching-cubes.md). By processing each tetrahedron independently, it guarantees a unique, unambiguous intersection for every configuration, producing a crack-free mesh without the need for special case handling [S1, S2, S3, S4, S5, unofficial].
