 ## Operating characteristics
 
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(N)$, where $N$ is the number of voxels. Each voxel is processed independently in constant time (6 tetrahedra, 16 cases).
+- **Time Complexity**: $O(N)$, where $N$ is the number of voxels. Each voxel is processed independently in constant time (6 tetrahedra, 16 cases) [S5, unofficial].
 - **Memory Complexity**: $O(N)$ for the scalar field. The output mesh size is proportional to the surface area. The edge cache requires $O(N)$ space if all edges are stored, or can be optimized by processing slices [S5, unofficial].
 - **Performance**: Generally slower than Marching Cubes due to more triangles generated (up to 19 edge samples per cube vs 12) and the overhead of tetrahedral decomposition [S4, S5, unofficial].
-- **Strengths**: Unambiguous, crack-free, topologically correct. No special cases needed.
-- **Limitations**: More triangles than MC. The choice of decomposition can introduce artifacts (bumps) along the diagonals of the cubes [S4, unofficial].
